From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:05:57 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 315/333] [ae-patch] Fix the fix-check findings on Speak
 replies (0314)

A code block phrase was spoken twice, once when its fence closed while
streaming and again from the final. It is now keyed by its place in the message
(the sentence before it), so the second occurrence is skipped and a later code
block after a different sentence is still spoken.

The spoken set was reseeded from every final already in the chat, so a reply
that said "Done." after an earlier "Done." went silent. It now holds only the
current turn's sentences: existing finals are marked handled and in-flight
sources start at their current length, and a send no longer carries the old
turn's sentences over (a late final of the old turn is ignored).

Fast answers no longer writes an effort after an await when the chat on screen
has changed or the chat is read-only.

A pending queue that is rebuilt (more than one entry added at once, or earlier
entries gone) is not counted as a send, and offsets for sources no longer in the
chat are dropped.

Added 2026-11-08.
